# A bare prelude VARIANT as a first-class function value (`xs.map(Some)`)
# CHECKS clean but CC-FAILs at build (the map lowering passes the variant as a
# value where the C signature wants a ctor call — `expected
# '__gg_Option__int64_t' but argument is of type 'void *'`). Pre-existing at
# base (verified 2026-07-20, pristine binary CC-FAILs identically); surfaced by
# the E_TypeInValuePosition scout, which EXCLUDES Variant from the reject so
# this shape keeps CHECKING (a variant ctor IS a value; pinned by the live
# check_gg_ok test). Filed in TODO.md: decide lower-or-reject (Core #10) — the
# intended output below assumes the LOWER ruling.
void main():
    Vector[int] xs = [1, 2, 3]
    Vector[Option[int]] ys = xs.map(Some)
    print(ys.len())
